  "raw_text": "Step 1: Determine the number of days in February.\nStep 2: Calculate how many times Suzanne walks in February based on the number of days and her walking schedule.\nStep 3: Multiply the number of times she walks by the distance she walks each time to find the total miles walked in February.\n\nFebruary typically has 28 days or 29 days in a leap year. We will consider both cases:\n\nFor a non-leap year (28 days):\nStep 1: 28 days\n\nFor a leap year (29 days):\nStep 1: 29 days\n\nNow calculate the number of times Suzanne walks in February for both cases:\n\nFor a non-leap year:\nStep 2: \\( \\frac{28}{3} \\approx 9.33 \\)\nSince she can only walk on full days, we take the integer part, which is 9 times.\n\nFor a leap year:\nStep 2: \\( \\frac{29}{3} \\approx 9.67 \\)\nAgain, taking the integer part, it is also 9 times.\n\nNow calculate the total miles walked:\n\nFor both non-leap and leap years:\nStep 3: \\( 9 \\times 4 = 36 \\) miles\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{36}<|im_end|>",
